# Runtime state. The database is the system of record for a live control plane, but it is
# machine-local: committing it would publish run history and make two checkouts disagree about
# which executions exist.
var/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Third-party binaries fetched for transport qualification are never re-published from here.
vendor/

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# Editor workspace files are per-developer.
*.code-workspace

# The maintainer's private working set, kept on disk and never published: the issue tracker and
# its generated report, per-agent instruction files and settings, and internal audit records.
.beads/
docs/reports/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GAUNTLET_AUDIT_REPORT.md
# Design history and working notes: the product contracts docs/PRD.md merged and supersedes, a
# study of a repository shared for reading only, implementation plans, tool-evaluation notes,
# and the maintainer's Obsidian vault settings.
docs/QUAESTOR_PLATFORM_AND_DATA_ARCHITECTURE_ORCHESTRATION_REVISED.md
docs/QUAESTOR_PRODUCT_DIRECTION.md
docs/QUAESTOR_RELAY_ARCHITECTURE.md
docs/ROSEN-BRIDGE-CROSS-EXAMINATION.md
docs/graphify-runbook-findings.md
docs/superpowers/
docs/upstream/
docs/.obsidian/

# Build artefacts from `pip install -e .`
*.egg-info/

# it would otherwise dominate every diff -- graph.json alone is 6.6 MB.
# The Obsidian export: thousands of generated notes describing the code, plus its
# core-plugins) is shared vault configuration and IS committed -- app.json in
# particular carries userIgnoreFilters: ["graph/"], which keeps Obsidian's own
# search and graph view from being swamped by the thousands of generated notes.

# Per-user Obsidian view state. The rest of docs/.obsidian/ (app, appearance,
# core-plugins) is shared vault configuration and IS committed.
docs/.obsidian/workspace.json
docs/.obsidian/graph.json
